# Deployment values for this device

This directory is empty in the image. It holds the values that belong to one
device and must never be part of a build.

## wan-mac

`wan-mac` holds the WAN MAC of this device, one MAC address and nothing else.

The 112 MiB partition layout has no `pdt_data_1` partition, so the stock
place where the base looks for the WAN MAC does not exist on this layout.
Read the MAC from the stock device before the layout change and write it
here:

```sh
printf '%s\n' 'aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff' > /etc/nx30pro/wan-mac
```

The value is used by the board script to derive the LAN MAC. Nothing in this
directory is read by the build and nothing here is committed to Git.
